frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,13,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,ui-key,subtitle,22,0,0,"Find albums by the upload day stored by iBroadcast, independently of release year. Dates are shown as stored, without a time-zone conversion."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,32,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1900,33,0,0,"Ragtime, brass bands and parlour songs filled theatres and homes, while cylinders and early discs carried performers to new listeners. In concert music, late Romantic richness met new approaches to harmony and colour."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,33,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1910,38,0,0,"Ragtime and dance bands shared the stage with early blues and, by 1917, the first jazz recordings. Concert music broke with tradition through bold rhythms and unfamiliar harmonies, and Tin Pan Alley songs travelled widely as sheet music."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,34,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1920,36,0,0,"Jazz, blues and dance orchestras reached growing audiences through records and the new medium of radio. Improvising soloists and expressive singers came to the fore, alongside the first country recordings, Broadway songs and adventurous concert music."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,35,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1930,33,0,0,"Big-band swing brought dance rhythms, memorable singers and inventive soloists to a wide audience. Film musicals, blues, gospel and country found loyal followings, and Latin rhythms such as the rumba found eager dancers."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,36,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1940,31,0,0,"Bebop gave jazz a fast, adventurous language as the swing era wound down. Jump blues fed into rhythm and blues, bluegrass took shape and crooners lent popular song a softer intimacy."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,37,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1950,40,0,0,"Rock and roll carried the energy of rhythm and blues and country to teenage audiences through radio and 45 rpm singles. Doo-wop, electric blues, mambo and modern jazz thrived as well, and the long-playing record gave albums room to grow."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,38,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1960,35,0,0,"Pop and rock became a space for rapid experimentation, from the British beat boom and folk-rock to psychedelic studio sounds. Soul, bossa nova, free jazz and the folk revival added a wealth of other voices."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,39,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1970,36,0,0,"Funk and disco filled dance floors, progressive rock stretched the album format and punk brought a sharper edge. Reggae, heavy metal, singer-songwriters and jazz fusion found large audiences, while early hip-hop and electronic experiments pointed ahead."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,40,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1980,41,0,0,"Synth-pop, new wave and the first house and techno tracks grew around synthesisers, drum machines and sampling. Music videos and portable cassette players changed how songs were seen and heard, as hip-hop widened its reach and rock and metal filled arenas."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,41,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,1990,38,0,0,"Grunge, alternative rock and Britpop gave guitar music fresh directions, while hip-hop and R&B became major creative forces. House, techno and drum and bass filled clubs and raves, and CD reissues put older recordings back into circulation."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,42,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,2000,32,0,0,"Hip-hop, R&B, pop, indie rock and electronic music shared an increasingly digital world. Downloads, digital music players and music blogs changed how listeners discovered songs, opening new routes for independent artists."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,43,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,2010,35,0,0,"Streaming and playlists changed everyday listening, bringing music from many places within easy reach. Pop, hip-hop and electronic dance music crossed paths, K-pop and Latin pop reached charts worldwide and independent artists built audiences online."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,44,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,prop,2020,34,0,0,"Streaming and short video clips connect pop, hip-hop and electronic music with regional scenes around the world. New releases sit alongside rediscovered recordings, bringing fresh voices and older favourites into the same listening space."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,51,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,return,,29,0,0,"Concert halls, opera houses and music at home shaped this era of classical and Romantic music. Recordings in your collection may revisit works written long before recording became widespread."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,52,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,return,,26,0,0,"Music from earlier centuries lives on through songs, instrumental works and performances passed down across generations. Explore the recordings that connect your collection with this period."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,53,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,return,,20,0,0,The music of this decade is still ahead of us. Explore releases associated with these future years in your collection.
frontend,src/tagcast/static/browse.js,54,"Browsing: artists, albums, tracks, browse groups, favourites",ui,string,return,,18,0,0,"Discover the music your collection connects with these years, from familiar styles to new directions and distinctive voices."
