frontend,src/tagcast/static/gapless.js,24,"Playback, queue, output, gapless, visualizer, queue sync",ui,html-text,return,,4,0,0,Supported audio and limitations
frontend,src/tagcast/static/gapless.js,24,"Playback, queue, output, gapless, visualizer, queue sync",ui,html-text,return,,73,0,0,"Use Original streaming quality (Premium) for consecutive FLAC album tracks: mono or stereo, 16/24-bit, 8–192 kHz, with compatible formats and decoder block sizes. Supported FLAC is repackaged without altering its audio samples. MP3 is experimental, requires reliable encoder timing metadata and is decoded to 24-bit PCM; sample alignment across real MP3 streams has not been established. Unsupported files or transitions use standard playback. No crossfade or automatic silence removal is used."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/gapless.js,24,"Playback, queue, output, gapless, visualizer, queue sync",ui,html-text,return,,73,0,0,The current file is prepared first. Longer tracks can start while the next downloads; very short runs prepare one extra track before starting. Buffer and preparation limits may switch to standard playback. The track-based time bar keeps the continuous buffer underneath. Volume and playback speed remain available in Playback options or Sound. Slow connections and incompatible files can still interrupt playback; this experiment does not guarantee uninterrupted output for every file or device.
