frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,61,0,0,"Off by default. This controls the discovery page and sidebar shortcut; bundled background texts on album pages stay available when it is off. Save to show 1001 Albums in the sidebar, then start an analysis when you choose. Compares the supplied 1955–2007 selection with your loaded album metadata locally. Results are saved on this computer; your iBroadcast library is unchanged."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,3,0,0,Open 1001 Albums
frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,2,0,0,Artist biographies
frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,5,0,1,Show artist biographies from TheAudioDB
frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,67,0,0,"Off by default. When you visit an album artist, Tagcast sends that artist’s name to TheAudioDB if no current local biography is available. English text is stored separately on this computer for up to 30 days before checking again. No library scan, iBroadcast changes or Last.fm account are needed. Biographies may be unavailable or refer to another artist with the same name; check the source link."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,2,0,0,Album information
frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,5,0,1,Show album information from TheAudioDB
frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,85,0,0,"Off by default. When you visit an album, Tagcast sends its album artist and full title to TheAudioDB if no current local text is available. English text is saved on this computer and checked again after 30 days, when revisited. Only one exact artist/title match is used; information is not available for every album or edition. Available 1001 Albums texts take priority even when the discovery page is disabled or has never been analysed; those albums do not look up or show TheAudioDB text."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/lookup.js,175,"Metadata editor helpers: credits, genres, online lookup, artwork",ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,3,0,1,Online sources & keys
