frontend,src/tagcast/static/theme-editor.js,38,Appearance & theme editor,ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,50,0,0,"Each theme has separate Light and Dark colours. Auto follows your system as before. Your draft stays here while you browse; saving is explicit. The built-in palettes are never overwritten. Warning/error colours keep their meaning. Native audio controls, system output pickers and window borders follow browser or operating-system styling."
frontend,src/tagcast/static/theme-editor.js,38,Appearance & theme editor,ui,html-text,ui-prop,innerHTML,82,0,0,"Contrast checks cover representative colour pairs, not every possible screen. Use the text fields to enter six-digit hex colours, for example #246276. Reset arrows restore individual colours. Import/export shares one theme as a small JSON file with its name, base palette and Light/Dark colour overrides. Export includes the current valid draft, without saving it. Import creates a new preview; choose Save theme or Save & use to keep it. Existing themes, account details and other settings are never included or replaced."
